        <li><b>Residences <small>06–22</small></b><span>83 three-bed homes with panoramic windows.</span><span class="pb"><i></i></span></li>
        <li><b>Roof <small>R</small></b><span>Walking track and an open-to-sky deck.</span><span class="pb"><i></i></span></li>
      </ol>
      <a class="feat" href="project.html?p=sm-axis"><span><small>Booking open</small><b>S. M. Axis · North Nazimabad</b></span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec tight" data-shape="logo" data-shape-x=".58" data-shape-y=".05" data-shape-s=".6" data-shape-a=".35" data-shape-ma=".15">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="legacy glass rv" data-spot>
      <div><b>1967</b><span>The year S. M. Group began its journey</span></div>
      <div><b><span class="count" id="yrs" data-to="59">0</span><sup>yrs</sup></b><span>Of building trust in Karachi</span></div>
      <div><b><span class="count" data-to="3">0</span></b><span>Landmarks: Burj Al Jinnah, S. M. House, S. M. Axis</span></div>
      <div><b>G+<span class="count" data-to="22">0</span></b><span>Floors at S. M. Axis, our newest tower</span></div>
      <div><b><span class="count" data-to="100">0</span><sup>%</sup></b><span>Electricity load backup at Burj Al Jinnah</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="landmarks" data-shape="plan" data-shape-x="-.62" data-shape-y=".1" data-shape-s=".6" data-shape-a=".35" data-shape-ma=".15">
  <div class="wrap mth">
    <div class="mth-l">
      <span class="kicker">Our projects</span>
      <h2 class="h2 split">Three landmarks. <span class="accent">One promise.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead rv d1">A serviced-apartment tower that's nearly ready to move in, a commercial address at Main 5 Star, and a new residential tower now open for booking.</p>
